# The Amazon EC2-compatible compute API (services/ec2/,
# .kiro/specs/ec2-compatible-api/). Sourced from the top-level Kconfig's
# "Service Modules" menu.

config EC2
	bool "Amazon EC2-compatible compute API (antikythera's controller)"
	default n
	depends on OPENSSL
	help
	  Builds the services/ec2/ module: an Amazon EC2-compatible API that
	  the AWS CLI, the AWS SDKs and Terraform's AWS provider can point at
	  to launch, stop, start and terminate instances, create and attach
	  EBS-style volumes, take snapshots and make VPCs and network
	  interfaces. The instances run on antikythera servers: this module
	  is antikythera's controller, sending signed commands and frames to
	  each server's helm over a mutually authenticated link. So far the
	  module holds the pinned botocore model, the generated operation
	  table, the coverage check and the ec2_node placeholder (task 1);
	  the codec, gateway, catalog, fleet layer and workflows follow.
	  OpenSSL is needed for SigV4 and the link's TLS. Off by default like
	  every new module (services/README.md). See
	  .kiro/specs/ec2-compatible-api/.
